# What NOT to upload to EAS.
#
# `eas workflow:run` uploads the whole project directory, and the OTA publish
# failed partway through that upload:
#
#   Uploading project archive to EAS (1.1 MB / 14.1 MB)
#   Failed to upload project sources. ... reason: read ECONNABORTED
#
# This project is maintained from a phone over mobile data, so a 14 MB
# single-shot upload is a coin flip. The archive only has to contain what
# `expo export` reads - app source and the assets it requires. Everything
# below is in the repository for other reasons and was being posted over the
# network on every publish for nothing.
#
# IMPORTANT: when this file exists EAS uses it INSTEAD OF .gitignore, not in
# addition to it. Everything .gitignore excludes therefore has to be repeated
# here, or the archive gets bigger rather than smaller - node_modules alone
# would dwarf the rest.

# ---- repeated from .gitignore (this file replaces it) ----
node_modules/
.env
.env.*
functions/.env
functions/.env.*
*.jks
*.keystore
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa
android/app/build/
ios/build/
ios/Pods/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log
*.tmp
/tmp/

# ---- not needed to bundle the app ----

# The marketing website. A separate app with its own operator logos in both
# png and webp, plus screenshots - the single biggest thing here that the
# bundler never opens.
mysheba-web/

# The admin console. Its own Vite/React app, deployed to Firebase Hosting
# (firebase.json target "admin-web"), with no connection to the mobile bundle.
admin-web/

# Cloud Functions. Deployed by firebase-tools, never bundled into the app.
functions/

# Build, audit and test tooling. Runs on this machine or in CI, not on EAS.
scripts/
.github/

# Native projects. Regenerated by prebuild, and an OTA update does not touch
# native code at all.
android/
ios/

# Version control and local scratch.
.git/
.easignore
